{"full":"hf:openai/privacy-filter","spaceId":"openai/privacy-filter","name":"OpenAI Privacy Filter","source":"huggingface","description":"OpenAI Privacy Filter ZeroGPU demo","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":78,"created":"2026-04-17T23:23:53.000Z","updated":"2026-04-24T14:39:09.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://openai-privacy-filter.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/openai/privacy-filter","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T17:24:09.360Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T17:24:09.360Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T17:24:09.360Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🛡️","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["OpenAI Privacy Filter is a bidirectional token-classification model for personally identifiable information (PII) detection and masking in text. It is intended for high-throughput data sanitization workflows where teams need a model that they can run on-premises that is fast, context-aware, and tunable.","OpenAI Privacy Filter is pretrained autoregressively to arrive at a checkpoint with similar architecture to gpt-oss, albeit of a smaller size. We then converted that checkpoint into a bidirectional token classifier over a privacy label taxonomy, and post-trained with a supervised classification loss. (For architecture details about gpt-oss, please see the gpt-oss model card.) Instead of generating text token-by-token, this model labels an input sequence in a single forward pass, then decodes coherent spans with a constrained Viterbi procedure. For each input token, the model predicts a…"],"features":["Permissive Apache 2.0 license: ideal for experimentation, customization, and commercial deployment.","Small size: Runs in a web browser or on a laptop – 1.5B parameters total and 50M active parameters.","Fine-tunable: Adapt the model to specific data distributions through easy and data efficient finetuning.","Long-context: 128,000-token context window enables processing long text with high throughput and no chunking.","Runtime control: configure precision/recall tradeoffs and detected span lengths through preset operating points."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f2535ec6301429781b55970c49b97976c97700643c0bc5f9814b02c9f9461713","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T01:02:53.284Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T17:24:09.439Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"OpenAI Privacy Filter is a bidirectional token-classification model for personally identifiable information (PII) detection and masking in text. It is intended for high-throughput data sanitization workflows where teams need a model that they can run on-premises that is fast, context-aware, and tunable.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"OpenAI Privacy Filter is a bidirectional token-classification model for personally identifiable information (PII) detection and masking in text. It is intended for high-throughput data sanitization workflows where teams need a model that they can run on-premises that is fast, context-aware, and tunable.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/README.md"},{"text":"Permissive Apache 2.0 license: ideal for experimentation, customization, and commercial deployment.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f2535ec6301429781b55970c49b97976c97700643c0bc5f9814b02c9f9461713","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T17:24:09.439Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-04-24T14:39:09.000Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T17:24:09.439Z